  "id": "cognitive-analytic-therapy",
  "term": "cognitive analytic therapy",
  "definition": "Cognitive analytic therapy is a brief integrative psychotherapy that combines ideas and methods from cognitive therapy and psychoanalysis. It works collaboratively and uses feedback, and it describes recurring problematic thinking patterns such as traps, dilemmas, and snags to help set a focused treatment aim.",
